---
import ImageSlot from './ImageSlot.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section class="section adapt" id="adaptation" aria-labelledby="adapt-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Built to keep adapting</p>

    <div class="grid adapt__top">
      <div class="adapt__copy">
        <h2 class="h2" id="adapt-title" data-split>
          The future of work is not a one-time redesign problem. <em>It is an ongoing adaptation problem.</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="lede adapt__lede" data-reveal style="--i:2">
          As AI capabilities evolve, workflows, roles, skills, decision rights, governance, and rewards need to
          evolve with them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="adapt__stat" data-reveal style="--i:2">
        <div class="adapt__orbit" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 200">
            <circle class="adapt__ring" cx="100" cy="100" r="88" />
            <circle class="adapt__ring adapt__ring--dash" cx="100" cy="100" r="66" />
            <g class="adapt__spin">
              <path class="adapt__arc" d="M100 12 A88 88 0 0 1 188 100" />
              <circle class="adapt__dot" cx="188" cy="100" r="5" />
            </g>
          </svg>
          <p class="adapt__num"><span data-count="2" data-suffix="">2</span>×</p>
        </div>
        <p class="adapt__text">
          Gartner forecasts that by 2028, organizations that establish continuous work redesign as a core
          capability will be twice as likely to sustain AI-driven work transformation. Gartner describes this
          capability as the ongoing adaptation of workflows, decision rights, jobs, and talent deployment as AI
          capabilities and business priorities evolve.
        </p>
        <p class="cite adapt__cite"><span class="chip"><Icon name="book-open-text" /> Gartner forecast, September 15, 2026.</span></p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="grid adapt__roles">
      <ImageSlot
        label="Roles, skills and workflow redesign session"
        src="/images/workshop-redesign.jpg"
        alt="A team working through sticky notes in a redesign workshop"
        ratio="16 / 10"
        tone="mist"
        class="adapt__img"
      />
      <div class="adapt__roles-copy">
        <span class="adapt__roles-icon" data-reveal><Icon name="arrows-clockwise" /></span>
        <h3 class="h3" data-reveal>Roles and rewards that support the redesigned work</h3>
        <p class="body adapt__roles-body" data-reveal style="--i:1">
          Where deeper redesign is required, I draw on my experience in workforce architecture to clarify how
          roles, skills, human judgment, decision rights, system access, governance, and rewards support the new
          workflow. The aim is to help people understand their contribution and give leaders a practical basis for
          adapting the work as AI capabilities evolve.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .adapt__top {
    margin-top: 28px;
    row-gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .adapt__copy {
    grid-column: 1 / 8;
  }
  .adapt__lede {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .adapt__stat {
    grid-column: 9 / 13;
  }
  .adapt__orbit {
    position: relative;
    width: min(260px, 100%);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }
  .adapt__orbit svg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .adapt__ring {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--line-strong);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .adapt__ring--dash {
    stroke: var(--teal);
    stroke-dasharray: 2 6;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .adapt__spin {
    transform-origin: 100px 100px;
    animation: orbit 9s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes orbit {
    to {
      transform: rotate(360deg);
    }
  }
  .adapt__arc {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--teal);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .adapt__dot {
    fill: var(--teal);
  }
  .adapt__num {
    position: relative;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(80px, 8vw, 116px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--teal-deep);
  }
  .adapt__text {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .adapt__cite {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .adapt__roles {
    margin-top: clamp(80px, 10vw, 136px);
    row-gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .adapt__roles :global(.adapt__img) {
    grid-column: 1 / 7;
  }
  .adapt__roles-copy {
    grid-column: 8 / 13;
  }
  .adapt__roles-icon {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 52px;
    height: 52px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid rgba(14, 116, 144, 0.35);
    color: var(--teal-deep);
  }
  .adapt__roles-icon :global(.icon) {
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    animation: orbit 12s linear infinite;
  }
  .adapt__roles-body {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .adapt__spin,
    .adapt__roles-icon :global(.icon) {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
